module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ClosedSubspaceFromQuasicoherentIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.IdealPullbackGenerators
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SmallEtaleBinaryProducts

/-!
# The inverse-image ideal over an affine chart is generated from one chart of the target

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a
big fppf site `B`, let `I ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals on the small étale site of `X` which is
cartesian on affine charts, and let `Q` be an affine étale chart of `X`.  Over an affine étale
chart `V` of `Y` carrying a morphism `v : V ⟶ Q ×_X Y`, the objectwise inverse-image ideal
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackChartIdeal` is already generated by the restrictions along `v`
of the sections pulled back from that *one* chart `Q`.

This is the second of the two hypotheses from which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf` proves
the opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8, and the one its implementation notes describe as open.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift`, with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift_fst` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift_snd`: **small-chart base change carries the
  binary product of two étale charts of `X` to the binary product of the base-changed charts**,
  in the form of the universal property that is used — a pair of morphisms from a chart `V` of
  `Y` into `Q ×_X Y` and `Q' ×_X Y` induces one into `(Q ×_X Q') ×_X Y`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict`: the structure map `f♯` commutes with
  restriction along a morphism of charts of `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_of_forall_restrict_mem_map`: **faithfully flat descent of
  membership in an ideal of regular functions on an affine chart** — a section lying, over the
  affine members of a covering sieve, in the extension of an ideal lies in the ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_of_isAffine`: for a sheaf of ideals
  cartesian on affine charts and a morphism `p : Z ⟶ Q` of affine charts of `X`, a restricted
  pulled-back section of `I` over `Z` lies in the ideal generated by the sections pulled back
  from `Q`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackChartIdeal_le_map`: **the objectwise inverse-image ideal over
  an affine chart `V` above `Q ×_X Y` is generated by the sections pulled back from `Q`.**

## Implementation notes

A generator of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealPresheaf` over `V` comes from some other
chart `Q'` of `X` through a morphism `w : V ⟶ Q' ×_X Y`, and the two families of generators are
compared over the product chart `P = Q ×_X Q'`, which exists by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.instHasBinaryProducts`.  The step the notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/IdealPullbackGenerators.lean` record as missing is the
morphism `V ⟶ P ×_X Y`: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preservesPullbacks_smallBaseChange` is
preservation of *fibre* products over an object of the site, and the small étale site of an
algebraic space has no terminal object, so it does not say that base change preserves the binary
product.  It is supplied here by hand, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift`: a morphism `V ⟶ Q ×_X Y` is the same thing as
a morphism `V ⟶ Q` of the big fppf site over `f`, by the universal property of the representable
base change, and under that translation the two universal properties — of `P` over `X` and of
`P ×_X Y` over `Y` — are the *same* lift, taken twice.  So no comparison of limits is needed, and
the two projection identities are `CategoryTheory.Functor.relativelyRepresentable.lift'_fst` and
`…lift'_snd` read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representablePullbackMap_isPullback_site`.

Once `m : V ⟶ P ×_X Y` is available, naturality of `f♯` moves the generator from `Q'` to `P`, so
that every generator is `res_m (f♯_P b)` for a section `b` of `I` over `P` with `v = m ∘ (P ⟶ Q)`.
The chart `P` need not be affine, `X` being only an algebraic space, so it is covered by affine
charts; their base changes cover `P ×_X Y`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows`), and pulling that covering
back along `m` covers `V`.  Over an affine member the comparison is the ideal computation
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_of_isAffine`, which is where
cartesianness of `I` enters through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsIdeal_le_map_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts`.  The conclusion
is local on `V` by the faithfully flat descent of `Ideal.eq_of_le_of_forall_map_le`, applied to
the ideal and to its sum with the principal ideal of the section in question; the faithfully flat
algebra is the product of the rings of a finite affine refinement of the covering, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.faithfullyFlat_pi_chartSectionsRing_of_ofArrows_mem_etalePrecoverage`.

Morphisms into a base-changed chart are handled through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bcLeft`, which is the underlying morphism of the big fppf site with its
codomain spelled as `CategoryTheory.Functor.relativelyRepresentable.pullback` rather than as the
chart `Q ×_X Y`.  The two spellings are definitionally equal, but the universal-property lemmas
are stated in the first one and `rw` builds its motive at a transparency at which the second is
not type-correct, so the spelling has to be fixed before any rewriting.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GF8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GF8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03G2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03G2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03ED](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03ED)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

noncomputable section

attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isContinuous_smallBaseChange

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-! ### Restriction of regular functions along a composite -/

/-- Restriction of regular functions along a composite of chart morphisms, in the spelling of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsRestrict`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRestrict_comp` over the other of the two spellings of the
ring of sections; the note on `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsRing` records why both are
needed. -/
theorem chartSectionsRestrict_comp (Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    {U V W : SmallEtale B S hS Z.1} (k : V ⟶ U) (g : W ⟶ V) :
    chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z (g ≫ k) =
      (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z g).comp (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z k) :=
  congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom ((smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Z.1 Z.2).obj.map_comp k.op g.op)

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsRestrict_comp` on a section. -/
theorem chartSectionsRestrict_comp_apply (Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    {U V W : SmallEtale B S hS Z.1} (k : V ⟶ U) (g : W ⟶ V)
    (x : chartSectionsRing B S hS Z U) :
    chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z (g ≫ k) x =
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z g (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z k x) :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (chartSectionsRestrict_comp B S hS Z k g) x

/-- The extension of an ideal of regular functions along a composite of chart morphisms is the
extension along the two factors in turn. -/
theorem map_chartSectionsRestrict_comp (Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    {U V W : SmallEtale B S hS Z.1} (k : V ⟶ U) (g : W ⟶ V)
    (J : Ideal (chartSectionsRing B S hS Z U)) :
    Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z (g ≫ k)) J =
      Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z g)
        (Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z k) J) := by
  rw [Ideal.map_map, chartSectionsRestrict_comp]

/-! ### Faithfully flat descent of membership in an ideal of regular functions -/

/-- **Membership in an ideal of regular functions on an affine chart is local.**  A regular
function on an affine étale chart `V` which lies, over the affine members of some covering sieve
of `V`, in the extension of an ideal `J ⊆ 𝒪_V` already lies in `J`.

The sieve contains a finite family of affine charts whose rings have a faithfully flat product
over the ring of `V`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.faithfullyFlat_pi_chartSectionsRing_of_ofArrows_mem_etalePrecoverage`),
and `Ideal.eq_of_le_of_forall_map_le` applied to `J` and to the sum of `J` with the principal
ideal of the section identifies the two. -/
theorem mem_of_forall_restrict_mem_map (Z : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS Z.1}
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Z.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    {T : Sieve V} (hT : T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS Z.1 V)
    (J : Ideal (chartSectionsRing B S hS Z V)) {s : chartSectionsRing B S hS Z V}
    (hs : ∀ ⦃W : SmallEtale B S hS Z.1⦄ (g : W ⟶ V), T g →
      IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Z.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W) →
        chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z g s ∈
          Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Z g) J) :
    s ∈ J := by
  obtain ⟨n, z, φ, hzaff, hzT, -, hzet⟩ :=
    SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_etale_ofArrows_le B S hS Z.1 hV hT
  let algz : ∀ i, Algebra (chartSectionsRing B S hS Z V)
      (chartSectionsRing B S hS Z (z i)) := fun i ↦ chartSectionsRestrictAlgebra B S hS Z (φ i)
  have hff := faithfullyFlat_pi_chartSectionsRing_of_ofArrows_mem_etalePrecoverage
    B S hS Z hV z φ hzaff hzet
  have heq : J = J ⊔ Ideal.span {s} := by
    refine Ideal.eq_of_le_of_forall_map_le
      (D := fun i ↦ chartSectionsRing B S hS Z (z i)) le_sup_left fun i => ?_
    refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 (sup_le (fun x hx => ?_) ?_)
    · exact Ideal.mem_comap.2 (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hx)
    · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
      exact hs (φ i) (hzT i) (hzaff i)
  rw [heq]
  exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self s)

variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : Y ⟶ X)
  (hf : yoneda.relativelyRepresentable f.hom)

/-! ### Morphisms into a base-changed chart -/

/-- The morphism of the big fppf site of `S` underlying a morphism of charts into a base-changed
chart `Q ×_X Y`, with its codomain spelled as
`CategoryTheory.Functor.relativelyRepresentable.pullback`.

Only the spelling of the codomain differs from `v.hom.left`; it is the spelling in which the
universal-property lemmas of the representable base change are stated, and `rw` cannot pass
between the two. -/
abbrev bcLeft {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q) : V.1.left ⟶ hf.pullback Q.1.hom :=
  v.hom.left

/-- A morphism of charts into a base-changed chart is a morphism over `Y`. -/
theorem bcLeft_fst {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q) :
    yoneda.map (bcLeft B S hS f hf v) ≫ hf.fst Q.1.hom = V.1.hom :=
  CostructuredArrow.w v.hom

/-- Composing with the base change of a morphism of charts of `X` composes the underlying
morphisms with `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.representablePullbackMap`. -/
theorem bcLeft_comp {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q) (k : Q ⟶ Q') :
    bcLeft B S hS f hf (v ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map k) =
      bcLeft B S hS f hf v ≫ representablePullbackMap B S hS f hf k :=
  rfl

/-- **The chart projection of a morphism into a base-changed chart is functorial.**  The
morphism `V ⟶ Q` of the big fppf site attached to `v : V ⟶ Q ×_X Y` by the cartesian projection
is carried, by composing `v` with the base change of `k : Q ⟶ Q'`, to its composite with `k`. -/
theorem bcProj_comp {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q) (k : Q ⟶ Q') :
    bcLeft B S hS f hf (v ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map k) ≫ hf.snd Q'.1.hom =
      (bcLeft B S hS f hf v ≫ hf.snd Q.1.hom) ≫ k.hom.left := by
  rw [bcLeft_comp, Category.assoc,
    (representablePullbackMap_isPullback_site B S hS f hf k).w, Category.assoc]

/-- The chart projection of a morphism into a base-changed chart is a morphism `V ⟶ Q` over
`f`, which is the datum the universal property of `Q ×_X Y` consumes. -/
theorem bcProj_w {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (m : V.1.left ⟶ hf.pullback Q.1.hom)
    (hm : yoneda.map m ≫ hf.fst Q.1.hom = V.1.hom) :
    yoneda.map (m ≫ hf.snd Q.1.hom) ≫ Q.1.hom = V.1.hom ≫ f.hom := by
  rw [yoneda.map_comp, Category.assoc, ← hf.w Q.1.hom, ← Category.assoc, hm]

/-- A morphism of the big fppf site over `Y` into the representable base change, read as a
morphism of charts into the base-changed chart. -/
def bcHomMk {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (m : V.1.left ⟶ hf.pullback Q.1.hom)
    (hm : yoneda.map m ≫ hf.fst Q.1.hom = V.1.hom) :
    V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (CostructuredArrow.homMk m hm)

/-- Two morphisms of charts into a base-changed chart with the same chart projection are equal:
they are both morphisms over `Y`, so the universal property of the base change applies. -/
theorem bc_hom_ext {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    {v w : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q}
    (h : bcLeft B S hS f hf v ≫ hf.snd Q.1.hom =
      bcLeft B S hS f hf w ≫ hf.snd Q.1.hom) :
    v = w := by
  refine ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (CostructuredArrow.hom_ext _ _ (hf.hom_ext ?_ h))
  rw [bcLeft_fst, bcLeft_fst]

/-! ### Small-chart base change and the product of two charts -/

section ProdLift

variable {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} {Q Q' : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)
    (w : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q')

/-- The morphism `V ⟶ Q ×_X Q'` of the big fppf site of `S` induced by two morphisms of charts
of `Y` into the base changes of `Q` and of `Q'`: the universal property of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.prodObj` applied to their two chart projections, which agree
over `X` because both composites with `f` are the structure morphism of `V`. -/
def prodChartLift : V.1.left ⟶ (SmallEtale.prodObj B S hS X.1 Q Q').1.left :=
  Q.property.rep.lift' (bcLeft B S hS f hf v ≫ hf.snd Q.1.hom)
    (bcLeft B S hS f hf w ≫ hf.snd Q'.1.hom)
    ((bcProj_w B S hS f hf _ (bcLeft_fst B S hS f hf v)).trans
      (bcProj_w B S hS f hf _ (bcLeft_fst B S hS f hf w)).symm)

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.prodChartLift` is a morphism `V ⟶ Q ×_X Q'` over `f`. -/
theorem prodChartLift_w :
    V.1.hom ≫ f.hom =
      yoneda.map (prodChartLift B S hS f hf v w) ≫
        (SmallEtale.prodObj B S hS X.1 Q Q').1.hom :=
  have h1 : prodChartLift B S hS f hf v w ≫ Q.property.rep.snd Q'.1.hom =
      bcLeft B S hS f hf w ≫ hf.snd Q'.1.hom :=
    Functor.relativelyRepresentable.lift'_snd _ _ _ _
  (bcProj_w B S hS f hf _ (bcLeft_fst B S hS f hf w)).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (fun t => yoneda.map t ≫ Q'.1.hom) h1.symm).trans
      ((congrArg (fun t => t ≫ Q'.1.hom) (yoneda.map_comp
          (prodChartLift B S hS f hf v w) (Q.property.rep.snd Q'.1.hom))).trans
        (Category.assoc _ _ _)))

/-- **Small-chart base change carries the product of two charts of `X` to the product of the
base-changed charts**, in the form of the universal property: two morphisms of charts of `Y`
into `Q ×_X Y` and `Q' ×_X Y` induce one into `(Q ×_X Q') ×_X Y`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preservesPullbacks_smallBaseChange` does not give this: a product of
charts is a fibre product over `X`, which is not an object of the small étale site of `X`. -/
def smallBaseChangeProdLift :
    V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj (SmallEtale.prodObj B S hS X.1 Q Q') :=
  bcHomMk B S hS f hf
    (hf.lift V.1.hom (prodChartLift B S hS f hf v w) (prodChartLift_w B S hS f hf v w))
    (hf.lift_fst _ _ _)

/-- The chart projection of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.prodChartLift`. -/
theorem smallBaseChangeProdLift_proj :
    bcLeft B S hS f hf (smallBaseChangeProdLift B S hS f hf v w) ≫
        hf.snd (SmallEtale.prodObj B S hS X.1 Q Q').1.hom =
      prodChartLift B S hS f hf v w :=
  hf.lift_snd _ _ _

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift` is compatible with the base change of the
first projection of the product chart. -/
theorem smallBaseChangeProdLift_fst :
    smallBaseChangeProdLift B S hS f hf v w ≫
        (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (SmallEtale.prodFst B S hS X.1 Q Q') = v := by
  refine bc_hom_ext B S hS f hf ?_
  rw [bcProj_comp, smallBaseChangeProdLift_proj]
  exact Functor.relativelyRepresentable.lift'_fst _ _ _ _

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift` is compatible with the base change of the
second projection of the product chart. -/
theorem smallBaseChangeProdLift_snd :
    smallBaseChangeProdLift B S hS f hf v w ≫
        (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (SmallEtale.prodSnd B S hS X.1 Q Q') = w := by
  refine bc_hom_ext B S hS f hf ?_
  rw [bcProj_comp, smallBaseChangeProdLift_proj]
  exact Functor.relativelyRepresentable.lift'_snd _ _ _ _

end ProdLift

/-! ### Naturality of the structure map on sections -/

/-- **The structure map `f♯` commutes with restriction along a morphism of charts of `X`**: it is
a morphism of sheaves of rings, read on sections over the charts. -/
theorem chartIdealPullbackHom_comp_restrict {Z Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (p : Z ⟶ Q) :
    (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Z).comp (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X p) =
      (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p)).comp
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q) :=
  congrArg RingCat.Hom.hom ((smallBaseChangeSharp B S hS f hf).hom.naturality p.op)

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdealPullbackHom_comp_restrict` on a section. -/
theorem chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict {Z Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (p : Z ⟶ Q)
    (a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q) :
    chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Z (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X p a) =
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y ((smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p)
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a) :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (chartIdealPullbackHom_comp_restrict B S hS f hf p) a

/-- Restricting `f♯` of a restricted section along `n : V ⟶ Z ×_X Y` is restricting `f♯` of the
section along `n` composed with the base change of the restriction map. -/
private theorem restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict {Z Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (p : Z ⟶ Q)
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} (n : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Z)
    (a : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Q) :
    chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y n
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Z (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X p a)) =
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y (n ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p)
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q a) := by
  rw [chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict, ← chartSectionsRestrict_comp_apply]

/-! ### The comparison over a morphism of affine charts -/

variable (I : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS X.1 X.2)).Submodule)

/-- **Over a morphism `p : Z ⟶ Q` of affine charts of `X`, the pulled-back sections of `I` over
`Z` lie in the ideal generated by the sections pulled back from `Q`.**

The sections of `I` over `Z` are generated by the restrictions of the sections over `Q`, because
`I` is cartesian on affine charts
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsIdeal_le_map_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts`), and the
structure map `f♯` carries that relation to `Y` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict`. -/
theorem restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_of_isAffine
    (hI : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := X.2) I.toSheafOfModules)
    {Q Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (p : Z ⟶ Q)
    (hQ : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q))
    (hZ : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Z))
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} (n : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Z)
    {b : chartSectionsRing B S hS X Z} (hb : b ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Z) :
    chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y n (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Z b) ∈
      Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y
          (n ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p))
        (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
          (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)) := by
  have hb' := chartSectionsIdeal_le_map_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts B S hS X I hI hQ hZ p hb
  have key : Ideal.map ((chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y n).comp
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Z))
      (Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X p) (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)) ≤
      Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y
          (n ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p))
        (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
          (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro a ha
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.comp_apply, RingHom.comp_apply,
      restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  exact key (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hb')

/-! ### The comparison over an arbitrary chart of `X` -/

/-- **A restricted pulled-back section of `I` over any chart `P` of `X` lying over an affine
chart `Q` lies in the ideal generated by the sections pulled back from `Q`**, as soon as it is
read over an affine chart `V` of `Y`.

The chart `P` need not be affine, `X` being only an algebraic space, so it is covered by affine
charts; their base changes cover `P ×_X Y`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows`) and pull back along `m` to
a covering of `V`.  Over an affine member the statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_of_isAffine`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_of_forall_restrict_mem_map` descends it to `V`. -/
theorem restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_map
    (hI : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := X.2) I.toSheafOfModules)
    {Q P : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (p : P ⟶ Q)
    (hQ : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q))
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1} (m : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj P)
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V))
    {b : chartSectionsRing B S hS X P} (hb : b ∈ chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I P) :
    chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y m (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf P b) ∈
      Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y
          (m ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p))
        (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
          (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)) := by
  obtain ⟨ι, Zc, c, hZaff, -, hZet⟩ := SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows B S hS X.1 P
  have hbccov := SmallEtale.ofArrows_mem_topology B S hS Y.1
    (fun i ↦ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj (Zc i))
    (fun i ↦ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (c i))
    (etalePrecoverage_smallBaseChange_ofArrows B S hS f hf Zc c hZet)
  refine mem_of_forall_restrict_mem_map B S hS Y hV
    ((SmallEtale.topology B S hS Y.1).pullback_stable m hbccov) _ ?_
  intro W g hg hWaff
  obtain ⟨i, w', heq⟩ : ∃ (i : ι) (w' : W ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj (Zc i)),
      w' ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (c i) = g ≫ m := by
    obtain ⟨-, u, -, ⟨i⟩, he⟩ := hg
    exact ⟨i, u, he⟩
  have hrestr : chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y g
        (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y m (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf P b)) =
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y w'
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf (Zc i)
          (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X (c i) b)) := by
    rw [restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict, heq, chartSectionsRestrict_comp_apply]
  rw [hrestr]
  have hmem := restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_of_isAffine B S hS f hf I hI
    (c i ≫ p) hQ (hZaff i) w' (I.map_mem (c i).op hb)
  have hcomp : w' ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map (c i ≫ p) =
      g ≫ (m ≫ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).map p) := by
    rw [Functor.map_comp, ← Category.assoc, heq, Category.assoc]
  rwa [hcomp, map_chartSectionsRestrict_comp] at hmem

/-! ### The objectwise inverse-image ideal over an affine chart -/

/-- **The objectwise inverse-image ideal over an affine chart `V` of `Y` above a base-changed
chart `Q ×_X Y` is generated by the sections pulled back from the single chart `Q`**, for an
affine chart `Q` of `X` and a sheaf of ideals `I ⊆ 𝒪_X` cartesian on affine charts.

This is the second hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf`, and
with it the opposite inclusion of Stacks 0GF8 needs only the affineness of the base-changed
charts.

A generator comes from another chart `Q'` of `X` through a morphism `w : V ⟶ Q' ×_X Y`.  The two
morphisms `v` and `w` induce one into the base change of the product chart `Q ×_X Q'`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeProdLift`), naturality of `f♯` rewrites the generator as
a restricted pullback of a section of `I` over that product chart, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_map` concludes. -/
theorem pullbackChartIdeal_le_map
    (hI : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (hF := X.2) I.toSheafOfModules)
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (hQ : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Q))
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS Y.1) (v : V ⟶ (smallBaseChange B S hS f hf).obj Q)
    (hV : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS Y.1 ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj V)) :
    pullbackChartIdeal B S hS f hf I V ≤
      Ideal.map (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y v)
        (Ideal.map (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q)
          (chartSectionsIdeal B S hS X I Q)) := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro zz ⟨Q', w, a, ha, rfl⟩
  have hgen : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS Y.1 Y.2)).val.map w.op
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q' a) =
      chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y (smallBaseChangeProdLift B S hS f hf v w)
        (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf (SmallEtale.prodObj B S hS X.1 Q Q')
          (chartSectionsRestrict B S hS X (SmallEtale.prodSnd B S hS X.1 Q Q') a)) := by
    change chartSectionsRestrict B S hS Y w (chartIdealPullbackHom B S hS f hf Q' a) = _
    rw [restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_restrict, smallBaseChangeProdLift_snd]
  rw [hgen]
  have hmem := restrict_chartIdealPullbackHom_mem_map B S hS f hf I hI
    (SmallEtale.prodFst B S hS X.1 Q Q') hQ (smallBaseChangeProdLift B S hS f hf v w) hV
    (I.map_mem (SmallEtale.prodSnd B S hS X.1 Q Q').op ha)
  rwa [smallBaseChangeProdLift_fst] at hmem

end

